REGIONAL REGULATION OF THE SPECIAL REGION PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF THE SPECIAL REGION PROVINCE

CAPITAL CITY OF JAKARTA

NUMBER 8 OF 2011

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

GOVERNOR OF THE SPECIAL REGION PROVINCE OF CAPITAL CITY JAKARTA,

Considering a. that discrimination and violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights and crimes against humanity, and are inconsistent with the position of the Special Region Province of Capital City Jakarta as the Capital City of the Unitary State of the Republic of Indonesia;

In view of

b. that in the context of fulfilling the constitutional rights of women and children and to improve the quality of life of women and children is one of the obligatory affairs that is the duty, authority, and responsibility of the Regional Government;

c. that discrimination and violence against women and children in the Special Region Province of Capital City Jakarta continues to increase and spread, causing community members to be unsafe in conducting their lives, thus requiring integrated protection efforts;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in point a, point b, and point c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children from Acts of Violence;

